WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.440
<i>I've got to deliver this oxygen!</i>

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:06.650
<i>The oxygen!</i>

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:07.730
<i>The oxygen!</i>

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.320
<i>The oxygen!</i>

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.450
If you keep pushing yourself too hard,
you'll end up going down first!

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.700
I can't leave you alone right now!

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:18.120
You come with me.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.620
Come with you?
But I have this oxygen to—

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.080
Just shut up and come!

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.040
See? Check it out!

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:32.050
Even if we slack off,
the body just keeps on moving.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:37.390
You have to take it easy once in a while
or you won't be able to work when it counts.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:46.520
Oh man... Work sure is tough, huh?

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:47.770
Yep.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:24.990
EPISODE 10:
STOMACH ULCER,
FRIENDSHIP, AND LOSS

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:24.990
Hey!

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.710
You're looking totally refreshed.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.920
Have you learned to game the system more?

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.630
Thanks.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.590
H-Hey, where's this coming from?

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:42.300
If it wasn't for you,
I could've self-destructed that day.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.890
Do you have to be such a straight arrow?
You're embarrassing me, man.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:54.940
Hey...

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.570
<i>As if we have any time to take it easy!</i>

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:02.450
<i>There's not enough oxygen to go around,</i>

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:04.870
<i>and that's why this body's
starting to disintegrate!</i>

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.200
<i>Don't you care what happens to this body?</i>

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.330
<i>If we don't keep working,
it'll be all over for this body!</i>

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.630
U-Um...

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:21.340
About the other day, I'm sor—

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.970
- Please forgive me!
- Huh?

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:28.810
I had no idea what shape this body was in,
and I left everything to you, Senpai.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:32.270
My classmate and I both feel terrible
about it, so since then,

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:33.850
we've been delivering
all the oxygen we can—

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:36.770
No! I'm the one who should
be apologizing to you!

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:41.900
I tried to take on the whole load
and ended up lashing out at you.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.240
I'm really sorry!

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.370
No! Please don't apologize!

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:49.750
Realizing that you have problems, too,
kind of set my mind at ease.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:50.370
Huh?

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.960
We're looking forward to being trained by you!

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.090
And I'm looking forward to it, too.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:05.090
Hey! Any Red Blood Cells out there
who have time to help out?

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.390
I wonder what's up.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:11.890
Did something happen?

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:13.520
This is an emergency summons!

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:17.150
We need you to go somewhere
with all the oxygen you can carry!

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.150
Where would that be?

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:19.610
The stomach.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:24.990
<i>The stomach.</i>

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.450
<i>Stores food that has been swallowed,</i>

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:31.330
<i>sterilizing it with the gastric acid
that it secretes from its walls.</i>

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:37.170
<i>In addition, it turns the food into mush
thanks to pepsin, a digestive enzyme,</i>

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:40.250
<i>carrying out the first step of digestion.</i>

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:44.470
This place is always such a sight to see.
The food's all mushy.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:49.430
Yeah. We'd get dissolved just like that
if we were to fall in.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:52.680
Not bringing the rookies here
was the right call.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.390
Hey you two!

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.480
Is this any time to be taking a tour?

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.440
- Oh, right! Sorry about that!
- Oh, right! Sorry about that!

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:02.400
We're not here to have fun!
Huddle up right now!

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:11.620
I'm not really a fan
of Old Man Gastric Chief Cell.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:14.870
<i>Gastric Chief Cells.</i>

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:18.540
<i>Cells that are prevalent in the stomach lining.</i>

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:23.090
<i>They secrete pepsinogen, the precursor of pepsin.</i>

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.840
I'm going to lay it out for you
from the get-go!

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:29.260
This is a blast furnace
where energy's extracted from food!

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:32.310
Right now, it's the most dangerous
place in this body!

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:36.270
I'm literally going to work you to death!

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:36.270
STOMACH

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:39.730
If you can't put your heart into it,
then get out of my sight this second!

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:43.110
For us Stomach Cells,

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:46.650
keeping that powerful gastric acid under control
is a job we risk our lives for!

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:51.620
MUCUS

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:51.620
But now, we're having
a hard time controlling it.

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:53.450
Look.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:58.210
An ulcer's developed in the stomach,
and the gastric mucosa's been breached.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:00.500
U-Ulcer?

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:03.800
Since the stomach's normally protected
by the gastric mucosa,

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:05.670
it doesn't get dissolved
in the gastric acid, but...

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:10.430
Now that the mucosa's damaged,
it's being eaten away by the acid.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:24.320
GASTRIC ACID
MUCOSAL LAYER
SUBMUCOSA
INTRINSIC MUSCULARIS
SUBSEROSA
SEROSA

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.140
<i>Stomach ulcer.</i>

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:16.770
<i>Occurs when the layer of mucus
that normally protects the stomach is reduced</i>

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:19.270
<i>until it's no longer able
to neutralize the gastric acid,</i>

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:24.320
ULCER

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:24.320
<i>which then proceeds to eat away
at the stomach itself.</i>

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:28.490
What the stomach needs most of all
right now is oxygen.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:32.530
The oxygen's not flowing well
because of stress, so it's unable to digest.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:38.660
Not only that, but the cells
who repair the mucosa need oxygen, too.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:44.130
If the serosa gets perforated, as well,
this stomach will end up melting down.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:46.050
So, whether we can stop that
from happening or not

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:49.130
will depend on how hard you guys work.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:51.760
I'm counting on you.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.140
Okay!

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.850
What's that old geezer's problem?

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:59.020
Who does he think he is?

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:01.940
Don't worry. It's just a bluff.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.520
It is, right? Just a bluff, right?

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.030
No.

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:10.700
That Gastric Chief Cell
isn't the type to play around.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:15.990
On the other side of the mucosa
is a sea of gastric acid, huh?

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:19.660
I can't believe anyone could work forever
in a scary place like this.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:24.670
The old guy's kind of a jerk,
but I'll give him props for at least that.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:30.510
Come to think of it, the reason we're short so many
Red Blood Cells might be because of this ulcer.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:33.470
The blood's leaking and heading that way.

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:38.520
You mean they fell right into the sea
of gastric acid? You must be kidding me!

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:43.770
<i>Emergency! The gastric acid-induced tear
has reached Area C-13!</i>

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:45.520
Tear?

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.230
Area C-13 is...

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:48.730
right here!

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:54.620
The gastric acid's eroding?

00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:59.250
Outta my way!

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.880
Subchief! Get that gastric mucosa fixed stat!

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:05.960
Copy that!

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:09.630
<i>Gastric Subchief Cells.</i>

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:13.260
<i>Cells that secrete the mucus
that protects the stomach</i>

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.890
<i>from being damaged
by gastric acid and pepsin.</i>

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:18.760
Platelets, close up the wound, will you?

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:20.770
Right, you don't have to tell us!

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.520
PLATELETS

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:22.640
Come on, guys, hurry it up!

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:23.520
Okay!

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:27.730
This is no time to get spooked!

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:30.610
If you don't want to end up
like that, get to work!

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:31.900
Okay.

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:37.830
<i>Platelets.</i>

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:41.330
<i>A type of blood component.</i>

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:44.120
<i>They assemble
wherever a blood vessel is damaged...</i>

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.880
<i>to block the opening
and stop the bleeding.</i>

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:50.210
You other cells do all you can to help out!

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:57.340
I hate to say it, but around here,
this is an everyday thing.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:01.680
Gorging on alcohol and greasy foods...

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:04.390
And on top of that, smoking and stress...

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:09.190
Those bad lifestyle choices reduced the gastric mucosa
which protects the stomach from gastric acid.

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:12.150
Is that also what caused the ulcer?

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:14.450
No, that wasn't the only cause.

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:15.650
Number one was...

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.410
Because of him.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:20.160
Him?

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:24.910
At any rate, sorry to have to say this
when you came out here to help,

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:29.380
but if you don't want to die,
then feel free to leave! As you can see...

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:32.340
you won't even get to die
a decent death here.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:38.050
S-Sorry, I-I gotta...

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:39.050
Huh?

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:41.890
Hey! Where are you going?

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.100
Nothing we can do about that.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:48.230
Having a spineless fool like that around
would only hinder us.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:51.440
<i>No.</i>

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:54.990
<i>He's worked just as hard as me until now.</i>

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:56.860
<i>I'm sure.</i>

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.870
What do you want from me?

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.410
I'm still scared!

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.630
My knees are buckling!

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:19.930
WHITE BLOOD CELL

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:24.140
What are the White Blood Cells doing here?

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:28.730
It's so messed up in here,
I bet it would scare off even the bacteria.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:36.440
Emergency!
A shock to the gastric mucosa!

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:39.110
Gastric acid erosion!
The lining will soon be torn!

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.570
What's this?

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.540
What's this shock?

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:53.670
The acidic gastric mucosa layer
is being neutralized by alkaline ammonia!

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:57.170
The gastric mucosa is no longer under protection,
and inflammation is about to ensue!

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:03.300
It's him!

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:07.680
They need oxygen and nutrients
to repair the mucosa!

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:13.270
Don't stop! Deliver, deliver!
We've got to stop the ulcer in its tracks!

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:21.860
If you fall from the wound, it's all over!

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:22.990
Watch out!

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:33.420
Uh-oh, the oxygen!

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.050
You...

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:43.220
I thought you'd run off for sure.

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:47.520
I happened to find the perfect capillary,
so I was just taking a break, that's all.

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:49.390
Why don't you head over yourself?

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:01.530
The ulcer has reached
the proper muscular layer!

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:04.990
VacA toxins are vacuolating
the gastric mucosa!

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:06.950
The mucosal layer has been stripped away...

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:08.910
and there's no stopping
the gastric acid erosion!

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:12.710
An enzyme that forms pores
in the gastric mucosal layer?

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:14.380
How did such a thing...

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.800
What the cell is going on here?

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:22.050
Hey, look! There's something over there!

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:30.350
Is that a germ?

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:31.890
No way!

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:34.100
No germ is that gigantic!

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:38.940
Not only that, but it can actually survive
in this sea of gastric acid?

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.570
That's right. That one right there...

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:45.280
is also what's causing this stomach ulcer.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:49.240
A bacterium that can survive even
in a place brimming with powerful acid...

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.250
H. pylori!

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:54.830
<i>Helicobacter pylori.</i>

00:12:55.290 --> 00:13:01.210
<i>It releases an enzyme called urease,
producing alkaline ammonia around itself.</i>

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:06.340
<i>This neutralizes gastric acids,
allowing it to survive inside the stomach</i>

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:10.930
<i>and damage the gastric mucosa
by secreting VacA toxins.</i>

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:14.520
<i>An extremely high percentage
of stomach ulcers</i>

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:17.770
<i>are thought to be caused by the presence
of this pylori bacterium.</i>

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:23.900
He's neutralizing the gastric acids with the ammonia
produced by the enzyme urease

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:27.240
to make it possible for him
to live inside this stomach.

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:32.830
He's planning to make all kinds of toxic
substances to damage the gastric mucosa.

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:36.040
Hey! Hurry up with the repairs there!

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:38.540
Wh-What kind of a germ is that?

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:44.760
Is that...

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.720
White Blood Cell!

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:47.680
Come on!

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:52.600
Don't let the pylori wreak any more havoc
on the gastric mucosa than it already has!

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:53.810
Roger that!

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:55.480
Get ready to die, you monster!

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:04.240
Whoa! Look out!

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:08.030
Come on!

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:08.950
Huh?

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:10.370
Let's deliver the oxygen!

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:12.370
Are you crazy?
When things are like this?

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:14.750
Isn't that why you came back?

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:20.000
Compared to what White Blood Cell and the others
are going through, this is nothing!

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.880
No way out of it, huh?

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:29.930
We're going to make a run for it, then,

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:32.600
since this is the last place
you'd want to loiter around in!

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:34.310
Are you ready?

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:36.310
Yeah. Our only option is to go!

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:39.400
Okay! On my count!

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:40.100
Three...

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:41.310
two...

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:42.270
one!

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:43.020
Run!

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:50.820
Dodge it!

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:04.750
All right, I'm good!

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:07.670
Okay! Here goes! There!

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:10.220
Okay, now it's your turn.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:11.470
Thank you!

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:15.930
Almost there.

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:18.680
- Watch out!
- Whoa!

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:21.310
Ouch, ouch!

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:29.530
Hey, are you all right?

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:33.030
I'm fine. It's no big deal.

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:36.200
We should turn back, after all!

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:39.250
I'm okay, I swear!

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:55.510
If things go south,
you tell me right away.

00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:58.220
All right.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:05.650
He sure doesn't know when to quit, this one!

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:08.480
I'm ending it now!

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:25.080
All right!

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:31.340
Unbelievable!

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:39.810
Aren't the tremors
getting worse than before?

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:41.890
Hurry!

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:43.850
The gastric lining's about to be destroyed!

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:45.730
Run!

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:56.660
Look out!

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:35.450
Idiot! You're going to fall in!

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:39.410
P-P-Please let me go! My friend!
I have to save him!

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:42.700
Knock it off!
Do you want to die, too?

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:45.330
Please let me go!
He's not dead yet!

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:47.040
I know he's not dead yet!

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:49.960
Let me go! Let me go!

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:54.380
Let it go! It's too late now!

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:59.090
Hey, this way!
Seal up this wound, will you, Platelets?

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:02.060
Okay, move it now! Everyone, move!

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:03.270
Okay!

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:04.980
Wait! Please wait!

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:07.520
Hey! Get out of our way!

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:11.020
He's... He hasn't come back yet!

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:11.820
He?

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:15.490
Enough already! Didn't I tell you?

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:18.030
This kind of thing happens on a daily basis here!

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:22.240
You can't get sentimental every single time,
or you'll end up putting the others at risk!

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:28.080
Hey, Red Blood Cells!

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:31.750
Quit your dawdling and keep that oxygen
and those nutrients coming!

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:32.380
Okay!

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:41.970
<i>Yo! Good work!</i>

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:47.690
<i>When it comes to White Blood Cell,
you totally go through this personality change.</i>

00:18:47.690 --> 00:18:51.060
<i>Look, you don't have to slow down
for my sake, okay?</i>

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:53.150
<i>Don't give me that!</i>

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:55.190
<i>Because of you...</i>

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:59.320
<i>I want to live just a little longer now, dammit!</i>

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:02.700
<i>Don't you remember
how you risked your life to save me?</i>

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:05.370
<i>I can't leave you alone right now!</i>

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:07.370
<i>Your face is a mess.</i>

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:31.600
Hey, what's that?

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:34.570
Is it attacking the pylori?

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.360
<i>Clarithromycin.</i>

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:39.780
<i>An antibiotic.</i>

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:44.660
<i>It prevents the growth of bacteria
by inhibiting their protein synthesis.</i>

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:44.660
DISINFECTION

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.370
I don't care what it is!

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:48.790
It's eradicating the pylori for us!

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.830
Attaboy! Kill that sucker!

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:55.290
You rotten Pylori Bacterium...
You can't croak fast enough for me!

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:58.300
<i>Pylori eradication.</i>

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:03.970
<i>Along with proton pump inhibitor therapy,
which suppresses the secretion of gastric acid,</i>

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:10.940
<i>two types of antibiotics, clarithromycin
and amoxicillin are taken for seven days.</i>

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:14.650
<i>Should any pylori bacteria remain after
this first-line elimination therapy,</i>

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:20.030
<i>clarithromycin is replaced with metronidazole
for second-line therapy.</i>

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:23.740
<i>Under these methods,
eradication is mostly successful.</i>

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:24.820
All right!

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:30.910
It will be easier to work
in this stomach now, won't it?

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:33.620
- It'll be the same.
- Huh?

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:36.840
As long as this body doesn't change...

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:41.090
neither will our work environment.

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:43.970
It will always be a code black workplace.

00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:51.980
Oh boy, am I wiped!

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:55.400
That was too much to take!
A beast-class bacterium like that one!

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:59.320
Huh? Isn't that the rookie?

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:01.900
Hey! Good work!

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:07.700
Can't he hear us?

00:21:25.890 --> 00:21:30.640
<i>I can't take your call right now.
Please leave a message after the beep.</i>

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:36.100
<i>Hey! How long are you planning
to skip work and laze around?</i>

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:39.060
ENUCLEATION CEREMONY

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:39.060
<i>We're super short-handed here!
Get back here!</i>

00:21:39.770 --> 00:21:43.030
<i>Hello? Hello? Are you there?</i>

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:41.570
I'm...

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:43.030
done.

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:47.570
<i>Hey, you can hear me, right?
I know you're there!</i>

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:46.490
I...

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:48.620
don't want to work anymore.

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:49.910
<i>Just get back here!</i>

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:52.950
<i>Hello? Hello?</i>

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:21.460
PREVIEW

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:23.460
A cell who can't work doesn't deserve to live.

00:23:23.210 --> 00:23:24.630
DESPERATION

00:23:24.170 --> 00:23:26.130
Due to a battle with an unknown pathogen,

00:23:25.210 --> 00:23:26.130
GOUT

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:27.970
each area is showing signs of inflammation!

00:23:28.220 --> 00:23:31.050
Do something about this work environment!

00:23:28.550 --> 00:23:29.800
REBELLION

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:33.970
Open your eyes, dammit!

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:33.970
DESPERATION, GOUT, AND REBELLION
